{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And Yosef was brought down.</b> It returns to the earlier matter, but it interrupted in between in order to juxtapose Yehudah's descent to Yosef's being sold — to say that because of it they brought him down from his greatness. And further, to juxtapose the affair of Potifar's wife to the affair of Tamar — to tell you: just as that one was for the sake of Heaven, so too that one was for the sake of Heaven, for she saw in her astrology that she was destined to raise children from him, and she did not know whether from her or from her daughter."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 39, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:02:42.712637369Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}